===Etymology 2===
From {{w|African American Vernacular English}}; due to lack of writing of slave speech, etymology is {{unk|en|title=difficult}} to trace, but it has been suggested that it is from {{der|en|wo|dëgg}}, {{m|wo|dëgga||to understand, to appreciate}}.<ref>Smitherman, Geneva (2000), Black Talk: Words and Phrases from the Hood to the Amen Corner (revised ed.), Boston: Houghton Mifflin, {{ISBN|0-395-96919-0}}</ref> It has also been suggested that it is from {{der|en|ga|tuig|dtuig}}.<ref>Random House Unabridged, 2001</ref> Others do not propose a distinct etymology, instead considering this a semantic shift of the existing English term (compare ''dig in/dig into'').<ref>eg: OED, "dig", from ME vt ''diggen''</ref>

